---
import MotionFigure from '../relational-motion/MotionFigure.astro';
import { routes, raftSteps, quorums, reads } from './model.mjs';
interface Props { kind: 'topology'|'routing'|'keys'|'raft'|'quorum'|'purchase'|'reads'; }
const { kind } = Astro.props;
const titles = {topology:'Portions down the page, copies across it',routing:'The request chooses the owners',keys:'What stays together under each key',raft:'From a proposed price to a successful reply',quorum:'A network split does not create two authorities',purchase:'Two replicated participants, one purchase',reads:'Two valid answers can miss one snapshot'};
const numbers = {topology:1,routing:2,keys:3,raft:4,quorum:5,purchase:6,reads:7};
const names = ['A','B','C','P'];
const owners = ['Customer shard A','Customer shard B','Customer shard C','Product shard P'];
const contents = ['Customer 1 · Mina','Customer 2 · Tariq','Customer 3 · Edda','P3 · P7 · P9'];
const r = routes.history.steps[0];
---
{kind === 'routing' || kind === 'raft' ? <MotionFigure collection="distributed/consensus" kind={kind} number={numbers[kind]} id={`dist-${kind}-title`} /> : <><figure class="dist-figure" data-dist={kind} aria-labelledby={`dist-${kind}-title`}>
  <figcaption id={`dist-${kind}-title`}><span>Figure {numbers[kind]}</span> {titles[kind]}</figcaption>
  {kind === 'topology' && <>
    <div class="topology" role="img" aria-label="Four shards, each with three replicas on machines 1, 2 and 3. Each row repeats the same portion; each column holds different portions. L marks that shard’s leader, F a follower.">
      <div class="machine-row"><span>Shard</span><b>Machine 1</b><b>Machine 2</b><b>Machine 3</b></div>
      {names.map((name,i)=><div class="machine-row"><div><strong>{name}</strong><small>{i<3?'Customers':'Products'}</small></div>{[0,1,2].map(n=><div class:list={['copy',n===i%3?'lead':'']}><b>{name}</b><span>{n===i%3?'L · leader':'F · follower'}</span></div>)}</div>)}
    </div>
    <p class="dist-note">Across a row: the same data copied three times. Down a column: different shards sharing one machine. L and F describe a role within that shard.</p>
    <p class="caption">An invented placement, not an engine configuration. The replicas add copies; the four shards divide ownership. Every machine stores a copy of every shard in this small model.</p>
  </>}
  {kind === 'routing' && <>
    <label class="option">Request <select data-route><option value="history">Mina’s order history</option><option value="report">Shop-wide paid-order line value</option><option value="purchase">Create purchase 103</option></select></label>
    <div class="router"><strong>SQL entry point</strong><span data-live data-route-label>{r.route}</span></div>
    <div class="owner-grid">{owners.map((owner,i)=><div class="owner" data-owner={names[i]}><strong>{owner}</strong><small>{contents[i]}</small><p data-live data-work={i}>{r.work[i]}</p></div>)}</div>
    <div class="result"><b data-live data-count>{r.count}</b> data owners contacted <span data-live data-result>{r.result}</span></div>
    <p class="explanation" data-live data-explanation aria-live="polite">{r.route}</p>
    <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 2 controls"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 3</span></div><div class="hold" data-hold><span></span></div>
    <p class="caption">A logical routing model. Customer records, orders, lines and payments have compatible customer placement. Products have a separate owner. Replicas, internal messages and any additional constraint or index participants are omitted. “One owner” does not mean “one machine contacted”.</p>
    <details><summary>All requests as text</summary>{Object.values(routes).map(route=><div><b>{route.label}</b><ol>{route.steps.map(s=><li>{s.route}. {s.result}.</li>)}</ol></div>)}</details>
  </>}
  {kind === 'keys' && <>
    <div class="key-lane"><strong>Ordered customer ranges</strong><div class="key-buckets"><div><small>Range A · 1–4</small><span>1 2 <b>3 4</b></span></div><div><small>Range B · 5–8</small><span><b>5 6</b> 7 8</span></div><div><small>Range C · 9–12</small><span>9 10 11 12</span></div></div><p>Customers 3–6 occupy two adjoining pieces.</p></div>
    <div class="key-lane"><strong>Hash buckets for the same customers</strong><div class="key-buckets"><div><small>Bucket A</small><span>1 <b>4</b> 7 10</span></div><div><small>Bucket B</small><span>2 <b>5</b> 8 11</span></div><div><small>Bucket C</small><span><b>3 6</b> 9 12</span></div></div><p>Customers 3–6 occupy all three buckets.</p></div>
    <div class="skew"><strong>The generated workload · 120,000 orders</strong><div class="bar"><span>Customer 1001: 84,000 · 70%</span><span>All others: 36,000 · 30%</span></div><p>Hashing <code>customer_id</code> keeps all 84,000 of this customer’s orders in the same key group.</p></div>
    <p class="caption">The twelve-key arrangement is illustrative; the displayed hash buckets are an invented mapping. The 70% count comes from the collection’s separate generated workload. Neither row count nor a balanced set of distinct keys measures request load.</p>
  </>}
  {kind === 'raft' && <>
    <div class="raft-status"><strong data-live data-raft-title>{raftSteps[0].title}</strong><span data-live data-reply>{raftSteps[0].reply}</span></div>
    <div class="raft-head"><span>Voter</span><span>Durable log →</span><span>Applied price</span></div>
    {['R1 · leader','R2 · follower','R3 · follower'].map((name,i)=><div class="raft-row"><strong>{name}</strong><div class="log"><span>Earlier</span><span data-log={i} class="missing" data-live>U absent</span></div><b data-price={i} data-live>20.00</b></div>)}
    <p class="dist-note" data-live data-agreement>R1 has not yet established commitment</p>
    <p class="explanation" data-live data-explanation aria-live="polite">{raftSteps[0].text}</p>
    <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 4 controls"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 6</span></div><div class="hold" data-hold><span></span></div>
    <p class="caption">A three-voter Raft model, with fixed membership and U created by the current leader in its current term. U means “set P7 catalogue price to 22.00”. Dashed means absent; a solid cell means durable; the agreement label marks R1 learning commitment. This is one partition’s command, not a distributed SQL transaction trace.</p>
    <details><summary>All price-change stages as text</summary><ol>{raftSteps.map(s=><li><b>{s.title}.</b> {s.text}</li>)}</ol></details>
  </>}
  {kind === 'quorum' && <>
    <label class="option">Connectivity <select data-quorum><option value="three">All three can communicate</option><option value="two">R1 isolated from R2 and R3</option><option value="one">Only R1 is reachable</option></select></label>
    <div class="voters">{['R1','R2','R3'].map((v,i)=><div data-voter={i}><b>{v}</b><span data-live>Reachable</span></div>)}</div>
    <p class="result" data-live data-quorum-result>{quorums.three.result}</p>
    <p class="explanation" data-live data-quorum-text aria-live="polite">{quorums.three.text}</p>
    <p class="caption">The same configured group of three voters; its majority is always two. “Reachable” refers to the communicating side shown. These are availability cases after any necessary election, not measured failover times.</p>
    <details><summary>Connectivity cases as text</summary><ul>{Object.values(quorums).map(q=><li><b>{q.label}.</b> {q.result}. {q.text}</li>)}</ul></details>
  </>}
  {kind === 'purchase' && <>
    <div class="purchase-participants"><div><strong>Customer shard A</strong><p>Pending order 103<br/>P7 × 1 at 20.00<br/>P3 × 2 at 4.50</p><div class="mini-copies">A₁ · A₂ · A₃</div><small>Agreement among A’s copies</small></div><div><strong>Product shard P</strong><p>Guard both decrements<br/>P7 stock 1 → 0<br/>P3 stock 12 → 10</p><div class="mini-copies">P₁ · P₂ · P₃</div><small>Agreement among P’s copies</small></div></div>
    <div class="atomic-bracket">↑ One recoverable transaction decision covers both ↓</div>
    <div class="outcomes"><div><b>Commit</b><span>Order + lines and stock changes</span></div><div><b>Abort</b><span>Neither owner keeps the purchase</span></div></div>
    <p class="caption">An independent replay from before purchase 103. Both product rows are assigned to P in this model, so there are two data participants. No payment is created. Each participant may span machines through its replicas; its own log agreement does not choose the joint outcome.</p>
  </>}
  {kind === 'reads' && <>
    <label class="option">Read contract <select data-read><option value="separate">Separate reads straddling the purchase</option><option value="before">Common snapshot before purchase</option><option value="after">Common snapshot after purchase</option></select></label>
    <div class="read-grid"><span>Committed history ↓</span><strong>A · order 103</strong><strong>P · P7 stock</strong><span>Before purchase</span><div data-read-cell="0" class="chosen">Absent <small data-read-mark data-live>Read 1</small></div><div data-read-cell="1">1 <small data-read-mark data-live hidden>Selected read</small></div><div class="commit-line">Atomic purchase 103 commits across A and P</div><span>After purchase</span><div data-read-cell="2">Present <small data-read-mark data-live hidden>Selected read</small></div><div data-read-cell="3" class="chosen">0 <small data-read-mark data-live>Read 2</small></div></div>
    <p class="result" data-live data-read-result>{reads.separate.result}</p><p class="explanation" data-live data-read-text aria-live="polite">{reads.separate.text}</p>
    <p class="caption">A conceptual schedule assuming an atomic purchase. The two separate reads may each be current when made. A common snapshot instead selects a compatible horizontal cut; the figure leaves its implementation to the distributed-reads article.</p>
    <details><summary>Read cases as text</summary><ul>{Object.values(reads).map(r=><li>{r.result}. {r.text}</li>)}</ul></details>
  </>}
</figure>

</>}
<script>
import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
import { routes, raftSteps, quorums, reads } from './model.mjs';
for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-dist]')) {
  const set = (sel:string,text:string) => { const el=root.querySelector(sel); if(el) el.textContent=text; };
  if(root.dataset.dist==='routing') {
    const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-route]')!;
    const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>3,draw:(n:number)=>{
      const s=routes[select.value as keyof typeof routes].steps[n];
      set('[data-route-label]',s.route); set('[data-result]',s.result); set('[data-count]',s.count);
      set('[data-explanation]',s.route+'. '+s.result+'.');
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-owner]').forEach(el=>el.classList.toggle('active',s.active.includes(el.dataset.owner!)));
      s.work.forEach((w,i)=>set(`[data-work="${i}"]`,w));
    }}); select.addEventListener('change',()=>{root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.click();player.render();});
  }
  if(root.dataset.dist==='raft') stepper(root,{steps:()=>raftSteps.length,draw:(n:number)=>{
    const s=raftSteps[n];set('[data-raft-title]',s.title);set('[data-reply]',s.reply);set('[data-explanation]',s.text);
    set('[data-agreement]',s.committed?'R1 knows U is committed · other copies may lag':'R1 has not yet established commitment');
    s.logs.forEach((has,i)=>{const cell=root.querySelector(`[data-log="${i}"]`)!;cell.textContent=has?'U · P7 → 22.00':'U absent';cell.classList.toggle('missing',!has);cell.classList.toggle('agreed',has&&s.committed);set(`[data-price="${i}"]`,s.prices[i]);});
  }});
  if(root.dataset.dist==='quorum') root.querySelector('[data-quorum]')!.addEventListener('change',e=>{
    const q=quorums[(e.target as HTMLSelectElement).value as keyof typeof quorums];set('[data-quorum-result]',q.result);set('[data-quorum-text]',q.text);
    q.members.forEach((on,i)=>{const el=root.querySelector(`[data-voter="${i}"]`)!;el.classList.toggle('unreachable',!on);el.querySelector('span')!.textContent=on?'Reachable':'Isolated / unavailable';});
  });
  if(root.dataset.dist==='reads') root.querySelector('[data-read]')!.addEventListener('change',e=>{
    const r=reads[(e.target as HTMLSelectElement).value as keyof typeof reads];set('[data-read-result]',r.result);set('[data-read-text]',r.text);
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-read-cell]').forEach(el=>{const i=Number(el.dataset.readCell);el.classList.toggle('chosen',r.picks.includes(i));const label=el.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-read-mark]')!;label.hidden=!r.picks.includes(i);label.textContent='Selected read';});
  });
}
</script>
<style>
.dist-figure{margin:2.2rem 0;font:.86rem/1.55 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text);--dist-accent:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 65%,var(--color-text));--dist-edge:color-mix(in srgb,var(--color-text) 54%,var(--color-surface));}
figcaption{font:500 1.05rem/1.4 var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:.8rem}figcaption>span{font:.66rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;margin-right:.5rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}
.topology,.owner-grid,.key-lane,.raft-row,.raft-head,.raft-status,.voters,.purchase-participants,.read-grid{background:var(--color-surface-alt)}
.machine-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.7fr repeat(3,1fr);gap:.6rem;padding:.55rem}.machine-row:first-child{font-size:.73rem;text-align:center}.machine-row small{display:block;font-size:.7rem}.copy{border:1px solid var(--dist-edge);padding:.55rem;text-align:center;display:grid;gap:.2rem}.copy b{font:1.4rem var(--font-serif)}.copy span{font-size:.7rem}.lead{border:2px solid var(--dist-accent);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 12%,var(--color-surface-alt));}
.dist-note,.caption{font:.78rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin:.8rem 0}.option{display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.8rem;margin:1rem 0}.option select{max-width:100%;padding:.45rem;color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--dist-edge);font:inherit}.router{text-align:center;border:1px solid var(--dist-edge);padding:.75rem;margin-bottom:1rem}.router span{display:block;margin-top:.3rem}.owner-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:.65rem;padding:.75rem}.owner{border:1px solid var(--dist-edge);padding:.65rem}.owner:last-child{grid-column:1/-1}.owner strong,.owner small{display:block}.owner small{font-size:.7rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.owner p{font:inherit;min-height:2.8em;margin:.65rem 0 0}.owner.active{border:2px solid var(--dist-accent);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 12%,var(--color-surface))}.result{padding:.9rem;border:1px solid var(--dist-edge);font:500 .86rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);margin:.8rem 0}.result>b{font:1.4rem var(--font-serif);margin-right:.2rem}.result>span{display:block;margin-top:.35rem}.explanation{border-left:3px solid var(--dist-accent);padding:.7rem .8rem;min-height:4.4em;font: .86rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);margin:.8rem 0}.controls{display:flex;gap:.4rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:.6rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt)}.controls button{border:1px solid var(--dist-edge);background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);border-radius:3px;padding:.45rem .65rem;font: .8rem var(--font-sans);cursor:pointer}.controls [aria-disabled=true]{color:var(--color-text-secondary);border-style:dashed}.controls>span{margin-left:auto;color:var(--color-text-secondary);font-size:.75rem}.hold{height:3px;background:var(--color-surface-alt)}.hold span{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--dist-accent);width:0}.dist-figure button:focus-visible,.dist-figure select:focus-visible,.dist-figure summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--dist-accent);outline-offset:3px}.dist-figure details{font-size:.78rem;margin-top:.75rem}.dist-figure summary{cursor:pointer}.dist-figure details li{margin:.4rem 0}
.key-lane{padding:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem}.key-buckets{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:.6rem;margin:.7rem 0}.key-buckets>div{border:1px solid var(--dist-edge);padding:.6rem}.key-buckets small,.key-buckets span{display:block}.key-buckets small{font-size:.7rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-bottom:.3rem}.key-buckets span{word-spacing:.35em;line-height:2}.key-buckets b{border-bottom:3px solid var(--dist-accent)}.key-lane p,.skew p{font:inherit;margin:.5rem 0 0}.skew{padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--dist-edge)}.bar{display:flex;margin-top:.65rem;min-height:4rem;font-size:.73rem}.bar span{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:.5rem;border:1px solid var(--dist-edge)}.bar span:first-child{width:70%;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 16%,var(--color-surface));}.bar span:last-child{width:30%;}
.raft-status{padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--dist-edge);display:grid;gap:.35rem}.raft-status span{color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.raft-head,.raft-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 2.1fr .9fr;gap:.6rem;padding:.75rem;align-items:center}.raft-head{font-size:.7rem;padding-bottom:.2rem}.raft-row{border-bottom:1px solid var(--dist-edge)}.raft-row>strong{font-size:.78rem}.raft-row>b{text-align:right;font:1.2rem var(--font-serif)}.log{display:flex;gap:.3rem}.log span{border:1px solid var(--dist-edge);padding:.5rem;flex:1;font-size:.73rem}.log .missing{border-style:dashed;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.log .agreed{border:2px solid var(--dist-accent);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 12%,var(--color-surface));}.voters{display:flex;gap:.8rem;padding:1rem}.voters>div{flex:1;border:2px solid var(--dist-accent);padding:1rem .5rem;text-align:center}.voters b{display:block;font:1.8rem var(--font-serif)}.voters span{display:block;font-size:.75rem;margin-top:.5rem}.voters .unreachable{border-style:dashed;border-color:var(--dist-edge);background:var(--color-surface)}
.purchase-participants{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.9rem}.purchase-participants>div{padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--dist-edge)}.purchase-participants p{font:inherit;line-height:1.8}.mini-copies{border:1px solid var(--dist-edge);padding:.4rem;text-align:center}.purchase-participants small{display:block;font-size:.7rem;margin-top:.4rem}.atomic-bracket{text-align:center;padding:.8rem;border:2px solid var(--dist-accent);border-top:0}.outcomes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;margin-top:.8rem}.outcomes>div{padding:.7rem;border:1px solid var(--dist-edge)}.outcomes b,.outcomes span{display:block}.outcomes span{font-size:.78rem;margin-top:.35rem}.read-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:.6rem;padding:.8rem;align-items:stretch}.read-grid>span,.read-grid>strong{font-size:.75rem;padding:.5rem}.read-grid>div:not(.commit-line){padding:.75rem;border:1px solid var(--dist-edge);font-size:1rem}.read-grid small:not([hidden]){display:block;font-size:.7rem;margin-top:.5rem}.read-grid .chosen{outline:2px solid var(--dist-accent);outline-offset:-2px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 14%,var(--color-surface));}.commit-line{grid-column:1/-1;text-align:center;border-block:2px solid var(--dist-edge);padding:.6rem;font-size:.75rem}
@media(max-width:550px){.machine-row{gap:.3rem;padding:.4rem}.machine-row:first-child{font-size:.65rem}.copy{padding:.4rem .15rem}.copy span{font-size:.64rem}.owner-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:.6rem}.owner:last-child{grid-column:auto}.owner p{min-height:0}.owner small{font-size:.75rem}.key-buckets{gap:.3rem}.key-buckets>div{padding:.4rem}.key-buckets small{font-size:.65rem}.key-buckets span{font-size:.78rem;word-spacing:.15em}.raft-head,.raft-row{grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.9fr .75fr;gap:.3rem;padding:.6rem .3rem}.raft-row>strong{font-size:.67rem}.log span{font-size:.65rem;padding:.4rem .25rem}.raft-row>b{font-size:1rem}.purchase-participants{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.8rem}.read-grid{gap:.3rem;padding:.5rem}.read-grid>span,.read-grid>strong{font-size:.66rem;padding:.3rem}.read-grid>div:not(.commit-line){padding:.6rem .4rem}.voters{gap:.4rem;padding:.6rem}.voters>div{padding:.7rem .3rem}.voters span{font-size:.7rem}.bar{font-size:.68rem}.explanation{min-height:0}}
</style>
